  "lineage": "Black-American male-quartet gospel tradition that emerged from late-19th-century Fisk Jubilee Singers university choirs and the parallel post-WWI Black Church male-quartet tradition — codified through the Golden Gate Quartet (the pre-WWII quartet, founded 1934), the Soul Stirrers (where Sam Cooke fronted before his secular pop crossover), the Dixie Hummingbirds, the Mighty Clouds of Joy, the Swan Silvertones, the Five Blind Boys of Alabama, the Pilgrim Travelers — most active 1930s-60s, with the modern continuation through the Williams Brothers and the broader gospel-quartet circuit",
